%S A398355 0,1,2,3,3,4,4,6,5,6,8,7,8,10,10,9,10,12,12,11,12,15,14,15,13,16,19,
%T A398355 18,19,17,20,22,22,22,22,21,22,24,24,24,24,23,24,29,27,28,27,29,25,30,
%U A398355 35,33,34,33,35,31,36,38,39,38,38,39,38,37,40,42,43,42,42,43,42
%N A398355 Number of previously visited grid points visible after taking n steps along the square spiral.
%C A398355 For the definition of the square spiral, see A400185. Whereas A400185 deals with a three-dimensional visibility question, this sequence only deals with occlusions in the plane.
%H A398355 Jonas Karlsson, <a href="/A398355/a398355.png">illustration of a(11) = 7</a>
%e A398355 After 0 steps, there is no previously visited point, so a(0) = 0. After one, two, and three steps, all previously visited points are visible, so a(1) = 1, a(2) = 2 and a(3) = 3. After four steps, we are at point (-1, 1) and we see the points (0, 0), (1, 0) and (0, 1), but (1, 1) is occluded by (0, 1), so a(4) = 3.
%K A398355 nonn,new
%O A398355 0,3
%A A398355 _Jonas Karlsson_ and _N. J. A. Sloane_, Sep 23 2026
